WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.702
CMMC is not solely a compliance-team initiative.

2
00:00:03.702 --> 00:00:16.074
The people who design systems, administer accounts, develop applications, manage contracts, operate services, handle information, and oversee suppliers all affect the security outcome.

3
00:00:16.074 --> 00:00:19.267
Leadership establishes accountability and resources.

4
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:31.679
Executives and program owners decide priorities, approve risk decisions, resolve ownership conflicts, and ensure that contract commitments are supported by realistic staffing, technology, and schedules.

5
00:00:31.679 --> 00:00:41.497
Contract and program teams identify clauses, information requirements, flow-down obligations, delivery expectations, and supplier relationships.

6
00:00:41.497 --> 00:00:46.476
They help technical teams understand what work and information are actually covered.

7
00:00:46.476 --> 00:00:57.082
Engineers and architects shape system boundaries, data flows, approved services, segmentation, identity, encryption, logging, backups, and resilience.

8
00:00:57.082 --> 00:01:02.819
Design choices can reduce scope and make required safeguards easier to operate consistently.

9
00:01:02.819 --> 00:01:11.889
Administrators and IT teams manage accounts, endpoints, networks, configurations, updates, monitoring, support, and change.

10
00:01:11.889 --> 00:01:17.936
Daily operational discipline determines whether documented controls remain true after an assessment.

11
00:01:17.936 --> 00:01:33.081
Developers and product teams contribute through secure development, controlled repositories, dependency management, testing, access restrictions, change review, and proper handling of FCI or CUI in development and support workflows.

12
00:01:33.081 --> 00:01:49.644
Employees need to recognize protected information, use approved systems, follow access and reporting procedures, complete training, and avoid moving contract data into unapproved email, storage, collaboration, or artificial-intelligence services.

13
00:01:49.644 --> 00:01:59.063
Security and compliance teams coordinate policy, risk, evidence, monitoring, incidents, internal review, and assessment activity.

14
00:01:59.063 --> 00:02:05.060
Their role is strongest when integrated with operations rather than functioning as a separate paperwork layer.
